# Graft — configuration
#
# Graft calls an LLM for concept nodes + per-symbol summaries, so the deep pass
# (`build --deep`) needs a model. The structural build (`build`, `check`, `ask`,
# `grep`, `map`, traversal) is deterministic tree-sitter and needs nothing.
#
# There are two ways to give it a model:
#   1. A SUBSCRIPTION — install the Claude Code CLI, sign in, and set nothing at
#      all. graft detects it and uses it when no API key is configured.
#   2. An API KEY — any provider. GRAFT_PROVIDER picks the WIRE FORMAT, not a
#      company; bring your own key.

# --- Option 1: your Claude subscription (no key) ------------------------------
# Requires the Claude Code CLI on PATH, signed in (https://claude.com/claude-code).
# Auto-detected when no API key is set, so this whole block is usually optional.
# GRAFT_PROVIDER=claude-cli
# Model alias or full id. Aliases track the current model, so prefer them.
# GRAFT_MODEL=sonnet
# Path to the binary, if it is not on PATH.
# GRAFT_CLAUDE_BIN=
# Per-call wall clock in ms (default 300000). GRAFT_TIMEOUT_MS is the
# provider-neutral name; this one wins when both are set.
# GRAFT_CLAUDE_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
# Per-call spend ceiling in USD, passed to the CLI as --max-budget-usd. Notional
# on a subscription: it is a runaway-loop valve, not a bill. A `--deep` build
# makes one call per file, so this bounds ONE call, not the run.
# Same thing per invocation: `graft build --deep --max-budget-usd 0.50`.
# GRAFT_CLAUDE_MAX_BUDGET_USD=

# --- Option 2: an API key -----------------------------------------------------
# Wire format / SDK: "openai" (any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) or "anthropic".
# GRAFT_PROVIDER=openai
# Your provider API key.
# GRAFT_API_KEY=
# Model id, AS YOUR ENDPOINT NAMES IT — the two spellings are not interchangeable:
# api.openai.com answers `openai/gpt-4o-mini` with a 404 model_not_found, and that
# `vendor/slug` form is OpenRouter's addressing scheme. Leave it unset and graft
# picks the right spelling for the base URL below.
# GRAFT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# Per-call wall clock in ms, all providers (default: the SDK's own).
# GRAFT_TIMEOUT_MS=
# Base URL for the "openai" wire format — this is how you pick a provider.
# Leave unset to hit api.openai.com. Examples:
#   OpenRouter:  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   Fireworks:   https://api.fireworks.ai/inference/v1
#   Groq:        https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   LiteLLM:     http://localhost:4000   (your proxy)
#   Ollama:      http://localhost:11434/v1
# GRAFT_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#
# Native Anthropic (no base URL needed):
#   GRAFT_PROVIDER=anthropic
#   GRAFT_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#   GRAFT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# --- Retries (all providers) --------------------------------------------------
# Retries after a failed call. Default 2. The right number belongs to the
# ENDPOINT, not to graft: raise it on a hard-rate-limited key (each retry waits
# out the endpoint's Retry-After, so a --deep build loses files instead of
# waiting), and set 0 against a local server that may not be running at all,
# where retrying every file 2× only triples the time to find out.
# GRAFT_MAX_RETRIES=2

# --- Deprecated (still honored as a fallback) ---------------------------------
# If GRAFT_API_KEY is unset, these legacy OpenRouter vars are used instead.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# GRAFT_OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini

# --- Graph location -----------------------------------------------------------
# Where the graph lives (default: <repo>/graft).
#
# USE AN ABSOLUTE PATH. A relative value is resolved against the CURRENT WORKING
# DIRECTORY, not the repo root — so `graft build` at the root and `graft ask` from
# a subdirectory would write and read two different graphs, and the second one
# reports an empty repo rather than an error. Only set this at all if the default
# location is a problem (it is git-ignored automatically).
# GRAFT_DIR=/abs/path/to/graft

# --- Benchmark (bench/) -------------------------------------------------------
# Per-role model overrides for the benchmark harness.
# BENCH_AGENT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5
# BENCH_JUDGE_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-4.8
